%description:

Tcp.mtuProbing:search -- host1 starts at the base MSS and raises the MSS by probes.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the path MTU search of RFC 4821, as Linux tcp_mtu_probing: 2 = from the
start of each connection, the sender sends single segments larger than its MSS and raises the
MSS when the peer acknowledges them; 0 and 1 = no search (1, the search after a black hole,
needs a detector that INET does not have)".

The classes: off (0, the default; 1 is the same, because INET has no detector of black holes),
search (2), invalid (below 0, above 2). The code: TcpConnection::configureStateVariables()
checks the value; with 2, TcpConnection::initMtuProbing() starts an active opener at the base
MSS, and TcpConnection::sendData() sends a probe larger than the MSS when the window has 11
segments; the ACK of the probe raises the MSS. This test separates "search" from "off".

Host under test: host1; host1 sends 1000000 bytes to host2; the path carries 1500 bytes, and the MSS of the handshake
is 1460 (1448 bytes of data with the Timestamps option). A frame carries 52 bytes of IP, TCP and
option headers more than its data: 1500 bytes of IP for 1448 bytes of data. Observation: level 1, the first data segment carries 1024 bytes, the
base MSS (1076 bytes of IP); later, a segment has more than 1400 bytes of IP. The search
stops when its range is narrower than 8 bytes, at about 1493 bytes.

%# parameter: Tcp.mtuProbing
%# class: search
%# value: 2
%# key: *.host1.tcp.mtuProbing
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpMtuProbingSearch")
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField == 1076B")
             .describe("the first frame of data of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField > 1400B")
             .describe("a frame above 1400 bytes of IP, after the search")
             .within(1.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpMtuProbingSearch compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.mtuProbing = 2    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 1000000B
sim-time-limit = 2s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpMtuProbingSearch: PASS
